---
import PushButton from "./PushButton.astro";
---

<section
  class="w-full max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 pt-12 flex flex-col gap-4 items-center"
>
  {/* Section Label */}
  <div class="w-full max-w-5xl flex items-center justify-center pt-4 pb-2">
    <div class="h-px bg-emerald-900/35 w-full"></div>
    <span
      class="px-4 font-mono font-bold text-base md:text-xl text-slate-500 uppercase tracking-[0.3em] whitespace-nowrap"
    >
      /* ABOUT */
    </span>
    <div class="h-px bg-emerald-900/35 w-full"></div>
  </div>

  {/* Terminal Command and Paragraphs */}
  <div
    class="w-full max-w-5xl space-y-6 text-base md:text-xl text-slate-400 leading-relaxed font-mono font-bold"
  >
    <div class="text-emerald-400 text-lg md:text-2xl mb-4">
      <span>[abdullah@abdullahs ~]$ whoami</span>
    </div>

    <p class="text-slate-200">
      I am a computer engineer, probably because I could never pick between
      hardware and software — I love both. My work has always lived at the
      bottom of the stack: the low-level stuff. Whether it's designing and
      laying out PCBs, writing RTL on FPGAs, or writing bare-metal C. And even
      when I move up the stack and touch high-level software, I stick to system
      languages — shout out to Golang — building software that directly
      interacts with hardware. Go microservices talking to FPGAs? Yes, please.
    </p>

    <p class="text-slate-200">
      I recently finished my Master's at UMich. During my last semester, I
      started working with Dr. Reetu Das on building a cycle-accurate hardware
      emulation for their recent <a
        href="https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3676641.3716267"
        class="text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-500 transition-colors underline duration-300"
      >
        PIM-based GPU-less LLM accelerator paper
      </a>. I didn't realize how much LLM decoding was bottlenecked by memory
      bandwidth and it sparked my interest in LLM acceleration and AI infra
      research. Now, I'm looking for PhD opportunities to contribute to solving
      LLM acceleration bottlenecks so that, one day, we can run large LLMs
      without needing a cluster of a million GPUs.
    </p>

    {/* Full About Button */}
    <PushButton text="Full About" route="/about" isDownload={false} />
  </div>
</section>
